    <item>
      <title>Reading A Definition and Roadmap for World Models</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/posts/reading-a-aefinition-and-roadmap-for-world-model/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:21:45 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/reading-a-aefinition-and-roadmap-for-world-model/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;core-content&#34;&gt;Core Content&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To give a comprehensive perspective and road map for wm, the paper provides:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;scientific definition&lt;/strong&gt; of a world model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;two-dimensional taxonomy&lt;/strong&gt; to classify existing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;staged roadmap&lt;/strong&gt; outlining the necessary steps to develop next-generation, foundation-scale world models capable of enabling Physical AGI (Artificial General Intelligence).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description>
    </item>
